-- CK-311: #954 (R-7.12: no input crashes the pass; it ends in a report).
-- A lambda applied directly to a function parameter, as in
-- `parse/good/Lambdas.beni`, overflows the stack of `dump
-- --stage=ownership` (`instCb` → `passOn` without end); `check` passes.
-- Red: crash. The golden is the report of the same program with the lambda
-- named (`twice f x`); the slice that turns it green blesses the real one.
applyTwice f x = (λg y → g (g y)) f x
